# PitLane Travel — Cursor compatibility

`AGENTS.md` is the authoritative repository agent / runbook.
`docs/product/day-70-contract.md` is the product, commercial, and stop-rule contract.

If this file conflicts with either of those, those win. Do not revive older
template rules that told agents to skip or ignore migration files.

## Hard rules

1. No destructive or irreversible actions. Never run `db:drop`, `db:push`,
   `db:rename`, `supasync`, or `supasync:include-all`, and never mutate
   production data. Richard's specific approval is required before any human
   considers those; even then, destructive / irreversible work is outside
   agent scope.
2. Ask first before schema or migration execution, dependency or lockfile
   changes, production data or seeds, provider configuration or credentials,
   payments or money movement, or any external send.
3. Schema work includes a migration. A fresh database needs both
   `npm run db:migrate` (journalled Drizzle) and `npm run db:migrate-sql`
   (hand-authored SQL 0003+). Do not skip `db/migrations`.
4. Do not invent live product capability. Do not enable money-moving flags.
5. Never print, commit, or log secrets. `.env.example` is the inventory;
   local values belong in `.env.local` only.

Import app code with `@/`. Prefer kebab-case names. Do not casually edit
`components/ui`.
